        "id": "au-holding-only-correct-extraction-is-enoug",
        "title": "Holding only 'Correct extraction' is enough to approve a carrier MBL/HBL",
        "body": "Step 18 says approving a document needs its own review right (document.review.approve). The Approve button calls review.approve, which checks that permission. But 'Save corrections & approve' and a document-type change call review.correct, and that endpoint only checks document.review.correct. It then finalises the document as approved (persistFinal writes a final extraction, sets status approved and stamps reviewedBy) and runs the approval hooks that start the B/L tracking job. A role given 'Correct extraction' without 'Approve extraction' can edit one field, or just change the type, and approve the MBL/HBL that way. The permission tree labels these as two separate powers, so an admin who splits them gets an approval the split was meant to stop.",
        "sev": "data",
        "pattern": "unenforced-approval",
        "note": "found by zyt-audit (unenforced-approval)"
      },
      "evidence": [
        { "file": "packages/api/src/routers/document.ts", "line": 661, "quote": ".use(requireNode(DOCUMENT.reviewCorrect))" },
        { "file": "packages/api/src/routers/document.ts", "line": 696, "quote": "const result = await persistFinal(context.db, {" },
        { "file": "packages/api/src/routers/document.ts", "line": 607, "quote": ".use(requireNode(DOCUMENT.reviewApprove))" },
        { "file": "apps/web/src/routes/_next/documents.$documentId.tsx", "line": 345, "quote": "reportNotices(result, \"Corrections saved and approved\");" }
      ],
      "reason": "unenforced-approval defect",
      "chain": false,
      "refute": "holds"
    },
